1
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Before Rambo... Before Oliver North...

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Walker is a drama, history, western film directed by Alex Cox.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
William Walker and his mercenary corps enter Nicaragua in the middle of the 19th
century in order to install a new government by a coup d'etat.

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
William Walker, played by Ed Harris.

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Ephraim Squier, played by Richard Masur.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Maj. Siegfried Hennington, played by René Auberjonois.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Timothy Crocker, played by Keith Szarabajka.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Captain Hornsby, played by Sy Richardson.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Byron Cole, played by Xander Berkeley.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Walker is a 1987 historical Weird Western film directed by
Alex Cox and written by Rudy Wurlitzer.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
It stars Ed Harris as William Walker, the American filibuster who
invaded and made himself president of Nicaragua.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The cast also features Richard Masur, René Auberjonois,
Peter Boyle, Miguel Sandoval and Marlee Matlin.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
An American-Mexican co-production, Walker was filmed
in Nicaragua, during the Contra War.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The film is intentionally full of postmodern anachronisms, such as helicopters,
Zippo lighters, automatic rifles, Diet Coke, magazines and cars.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Joe Strummer, formerly of the Clash, scored the film.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Walker was released by Universal Pictures on December 4, 1987 to generally polarized reviews and grossed
nearly $300,000 against a production budget of $6 million, becoming a box-office bomb.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The film explores themes of small town, cannon, sword, mexican standoff, horse.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The tone is emotional.
